<title>USA: Western Resources sees gain from ADT shares.</title>
<headline>Western Resources sees gain from ADT shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOPEKA, Kan. 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Resources Inc said Wednesday it has a potential pretax gain of more than $800 million resulting from its investment in 38 million shares of ADT Ltd common stock.</p>
<p>The ADT stock converted to about 18.4 million shares of Tyco International Inc shares on July 2. Tyco and ADT merged on that date.  </p>
<p>Western Resources, which made an original investment of about $590 million in the stock, said it sold five million shares of Tyco stock for $387 million. It now holds about 13.5 million shares of Tyco currently valued at about $1.1 billion, based on Tyco's share price as of July 28.</p>
<p>Tyco shares on Wednesday were up 7/16 at 80-5/8.</p>
<p>Western Resources shares rose 1/16 to 34-3/16.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
